  "note": "Annual election of six urban councillors, January 1932; only three retiring members sought re-election and there was no contest (Belfast Telegraph, 6 January 1932, p. 2). Thomas Loughridge, Walter M'Keown and James M'Cartney did not seek re-election; the paper says they may be co-opted at a later date. Returned unopposed."
